# Milestone: M6
# Covers: Phase 2 atom-method dispatch — slot lookup starting from a
# non-UVAL_OBJECT receiver routes through the realm-global atom proto
# (Integer / String / etc.).
#
# This fixture installs a slot on an atom proto via `Atom.slot = v` and
# verifies the slot is reachable via `<literal>.slot`.  Without
# atom-method dispatch (pre-Phase 2), the literal lookup would error
# with "GETSLOT: receiver is not an Object" before atom-routing existed.
#
# Float-literal coverage is deferred: the v1.0 lexer does not currently
# emit a single TOK_FLOAT for `3.14`; literal `3.14.fmark` parses as
# `(3 . 14) . fmark` and fails before atom dispatch.  Int + String are
# sufficient to validate the dispatch-arm wiring.

# Stash a slot on Integer that we can resolve from any int literal.
Integer.marker = 42
[00000000] 42

1.marker
[00000001] 42

99.marker
[00000002] 42

# Symmetric for String.
String.smark = 200
[00000003] 200

"abc".smark
[00000004] 200
